1yd0|v|To weigh or measure according to a scale; to measure; also, to grade or vary according to a scale or system. ; To strip or clear of scale or scales; as, to scale a fish; to scale the inside of a boiler. ; To take off in thin layers or scales, as tartar from the teeth; to pare off, as a surface. ; To scatter; to spread. ; To clean, as the inside of a cannon, by the explosion of a small quantity of powder. ; To separate and come off in thin layers or laminae; as, some sandstone scales by exposure. ; To separate; to scatter. ; To climb by a ladder, or as if by a ladder; to ascend by steps or by climbing; to clamber up; as, to scale the wall of a fort. ; To lead up by steps; to ascend.	o:1r52,14,1~1r52,14,1	D:1a2b,47,2;1ph3,27,4;2g4b,8,24~2g4b,8,24;1ph3,27,4;1a2b,47,2
