1yw4|n|An instrument with which anything is scraped. ; An instrument by which the soles of shoes are cleaned from mud and the like, by drawing them across it. ; An instrument drawn by oxen or horses, used for scraping up earth in making or repairing roads, digging cellars, canals etc. ; An instrument having two or three sharp sides or edges, for cleaning the planks, masts, or decks of a ship. ; In the printing press, a board, or blade, the edge of which is made to rub over the tympan sheet and thus produce the impression. ; One who scrapes. ; One who plays awkwardly on a violin. ; One who acquires avariciously and saves penuriously.	a:1ogt,74,2;2g08,59,3~2g08,59,3;1ogt,74,2	V:8q0,98,1~8q0,98,1	n:1ko0,110,5;2g08,54,2~1ko0,110,5;2g08,54,2	N:8q0,114,3~8q0,114,3
